    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c12a091c_2fa91666",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 925,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T18:51:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hmm, the size overhead is ~4k for plat_file_context, which has ~500 entries. I guess link list will also introduce some overhead. How about the dynamic sized allocation:\n\nint array_size \u003d 8;\nconst struct spec **result \u003d calloc(array_size, sizeof(struct spec*));\n.....\nif (match_count) {\n  result[*match_count] \u003d spec;\n  *match_count +\u003d 1;\n  if (*match_count \u003e\u003d array_size) {\n    array_size *\u003d 2;\n    result \u003d realloc(result, array_size * size of(struct spec*));\n    // check result and memset extended area to 0.\n  }\n\n  continue;\n}",
      "parentUuid": "4c5884ef_fa4e8cc8",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "975b5099_d7ab65e2",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 925,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010111
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T19:01:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was questioning the approach of doing this allocation at all in the common code path even though we usually only want a single match.  Splitting it into two functions with a common helper might be preferable.",
      "parentUuid": "c12a091c_2fa91666",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
