    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e2c092b_4c33aceb",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010111
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T14:08:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the basis for including/excluding information from the hash?  For example, here we omit the type_str aka the mode, so we aren\u0027t including everything from the matching entry in file_contexts.  OTOH, since we knew it was a match, do we need anything besides the actual contexts here?  The question we are trying to answer is could the context on files within this directory change?",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b6315b9_04c7c1e9",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T18:38:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am tying to hash the actually lines in the file_context file. e.g.\n/data(/.*)?\t\tu:object_r:system_data_file:s0\n/data/.layout_version\t\tu:object_r:install_data_file:s0\n/data/unencrypted(/.*)?         u:object_r:unencrypted_data_file:s0\n/data/backup(/.*)?\t\tu:object_r:backup_data_file:s0\n/data/secure/backup(/.*)?\tu:object_r:backup_data_file:s0\n/data/system/ndebugsocket\tu:object_r:system_ndebug_socket:s0\n\n\nSo the regex_str and ctx_raw are directly read from the file, while other fields are intermediate attributes. Since it\u0027s more difficult to reference the actually line contents in the file, I just use \"regex_str+ctx_raw\" as the base information.",
      "parentUuid": "3e2c092b_4c33aceb",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c42d26c_beac1cd7",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T18:48:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to hash the context (as line 1042 currently does), since we want the hash to be invalidated if the file label changes (but not the file regex).\n\nStephen has a good point about also hashing matches[i]-\u003emode (aka \"file type\").\n\nPer \"man ./external/selinux/libselinux/man/man5/selabel_file.5\"\n\n  File_type\n  An optional file type consisting of:\n  -b - Block Device -c - Character Device \n  -d - Directory -p - Named Pipe \n  -l - Symbolic Link -s - Socket \n  -- - Ordinary file\n\nWe don\u0027t use this much in Android\u0027s SELinux policy, but we should still include it as part of the hash.",
      "parentUuid": "6b6315b9_04c7c1e9",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6ad7d76_b492c339",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T18:51:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack",
      "parentUuid": "5c42d26c_beac1cd7",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf87c31a_247d8df1",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010111
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T19:01:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to hash the regex_str and type_str at all?  We know that they matched this key since they were returned by lookup_all(). So then the only thing that matters is whether any matching entry yields a different security context, right?  So we only need to hash the context strings and we\u0027re done?",
      "parentUuid": "a6ad7d76_b492c339",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e39eb5d_408191b5",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T19:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But we might have a different entry in the matched subset since it\u0027s a partial match.\nif\n/data/test(/.*)? u:object_r:system_data_file:s0\nchanges to \n/data/test/dir(/.*)? u:object_r:system_data_file:s0\n\nand /data/test/dir1 will match both entries, and the hash stays the same. Sounds a bit risky to me?",
      "parentUuid": "bf87c31a_247d8df1",
      "revId": "ce7653a0e086635bb0d66eef834ff99a32d60492",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5b50333_f2d390c8",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-04T19:57:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, removed the regex. Don\u0027t add mode/type for the similar reason. (We won\u0027t do a regex match unless the type already matches.)",
      "parentUuid": "1e39eb5d_408191b5",
